{{fbdoc item="title" value="__FB_MIPS__"}}----
Intrinsic define shared by 32-bit and 64-bit MIPS targets.

{{fbdoc item="syntax"}}
	""__FB_MIPS__""

{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	Define without a value created at compile time for every MIPS CPU-family target.  The compiler also defines exactly one of ##[[KeyPgDdfbmips32|__FB_MIPS32__]]## or ##[[KeyPgDdfbmips64|__FB_MIPS64__]]##.  Big-endian MIPS targets additionally define ##[[KeyPgDdFBBigEndian|__FB_BIGENDIAN__]]##.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
%%(freebasic)
#ifdef __FB_MIPS__
	print "MIPS target"
#endif
%%

{{fbdoc item="ver"}}
	- Since fbc 1.20.3

{{fbdoc item="see"}}
	- ##[[KeyPgDdfbmips32|__FB_MIPS32__]]##
	- ##[[KeyPgDdfbmips64|__FB_MIPS64__]]##
	- ##[[CompilerOpttarget|Compiler Option: -target]]##

